/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - At failure the concrete in a short column is at its design compressive strength and the steel has yielded.
   - Pu is the factored axial load in N; fck and fy are the characteristic strengths of concrete and steel in N/mm²; Ag is the gross area, Asc the area of longitudinal steel and Ac the net concrete area, all in mm².
   - The formula is valid only when emin does not exceed 0.05 times the lateral dimension.
   - Design steps: (1) write Pu, fck, fy and Ag; (2) check that the column is short and emin ≤ 0.05D; (3) find Asc from the formula and raise it to 0.8 % if smaller; (4) choose bars and check the capacity with the bars provided; (5) choose the t
   - A closely spaced helix confines the concrete core.
   - Vhelix and Vcore are the volumes of helix steel and of core concrete per unit height; Ak = πDk²/4 is the core area, Dk being the core diameter measured to the outside of the helix.
   - The helix pitch must be not more than 75 mm and not more than Dk/6, and not less than 25 mm or 3 times the helix bar diameter.
*/
